  "clips": [
    {
      "file": "ru/CH04_P04_L001_ru.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L001",
      "language": "ru",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F01",
      "reading_order": 1,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_004",
      "role": "narrator",
      "kind": "narration",
      "voice_id": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "Во время полёта профессор решил изучить образцы, полученные на Археоне.",
      "emotion_tag": "[with curiosity]",
      "duration_ms": 5040,
      "sha256": "971bcd6c07aa40b9813db748df592fa7086766353db9693c987893d73b48e903"
    },
    {
      "file": "ru/CH04_P04_L002_ru.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L002",
      "language": "ru",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F01",
      "reading_order": 2,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_001",
      "role": "mika",
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "voice_id": "XjcBo3s44Dqh64FhOpGk",
      "text": "Что там?",
      "emotion_tag": "[curious]",
      "duration_ms": 1040,
      "sha256": "2d91fd9410be5e81c98fafdc06cfb1ce5ba1c4915c8c829d0d9dd2267444cf78"
    },
    {
      "file": "ru/CH04_P04_L003_ru.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L003",
      "language": "ru",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F02",
      "reading_order": 3,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_015",
      "role": "professor",
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "voice_id": "pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4",
      "text": "Кажется, я знаю, откуда они!",
      "emotion_tag": "[excited realization]",
      "duration_ms": 2320,
      "sha256": "f1768148b44b6d6247fb28ac61187aae86a6a706c53ab4dea7485379dcb6d338"
    },
    {
      "file": "ru/CH04_P04_L004_ru.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L004",
      "language": "ru",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F03",
      "reading_order": 4,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_015",
      "role": "professor",
      "kind": "science_explanation",
      "voice_id": "pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4",
      "text": "Их ДНК удивительно похожа на ДНК древних земных рептилий!",
      "emotion_tag": "[with scientific wonder]",
      "duration_ms": 4960,
      "sha256": "e0f694e44c0998edb1d4c07ab2d170f0fa228feb41cca92fae7f07943302b96f"
    },
    {
      "file": "ru/CH04_P04_L005_ru.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L005",
      "language": "ru",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F04",
      "reading_order": 5,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_015",
      "role": "professor",
      "kind": "flashback_explanation",
      "voice_id": "pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4",
      "text": "65–70 миллионов лет назад Землю населяли гигантские ящероподобные существа — динозавры.",
      "emotion_tag": "[storytelling, fascinated]",
      "duration_ms": 8800,
      "sha256": "a4a4c5cf58bdc9471aa01e4fededbc4528bad14c05d8633cc15f5130c86d3abe"
    },
    {
      "file": "ru/CH04_P04_L006_ru.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L006",
      "language": "ru",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F05",
      "reading_order": 6,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_015",
      "role": "professor",
      "kind": "flashback_explanation",
      "voice_id": "pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4",
      "text": "Но около 66 миллионов лет назад удар огромного астероида изменил всё. Большинство динозавров исчезло, и открылись новые пути эволюции млекопитающих, а позднее — человека.",
      "emotion_tag": "[serious, thoughtful]",
      "duration_ms": 14080,
      "sha256": "b340a2c985f75d7a32bf9670808fe571a147fcd026a7bc40a3b9e0b603fdf493"
    },
    {
      "file": "en/CH04_P04_L001_en.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L001",
      "language": "en",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F01",
      "reading_order": 1,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_004",
      "role": "narrator",
      "kind": "narration",
      "voice_id": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "During the flight, the professor decided to examine the samples collected on Archeon.",
      "emotion_tag": "[with curiosity]",
      "duration_ms": 5040,
      "sha256": "5d445801db0fbc36af0eec8efab6e740eed2aba7555639590536b25262769c9a"
    },
    {
      "file": "en/CH04_P04_L002_en.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L002",
      "language": "en",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F01",
      "reading_order": 2,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_001",
      "role": "mika",
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "voice_id": "XjcBo3s44Dqh64FhOpGk",
      "text": "What is it?",
      "emotion_tag": "[curious]",
      "duration_ms": 1120,
      "sha256": "413ae96d5e398518fd13b0df7220aaf9a3ac6b4d062d1dd365c2175e9c1e3787"
    },
    {
      "file": "en/CH04_P04_L003_en.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L003",
      "language": "en",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F02",
      "reading_order": 3,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_015",
      "role": "professor",
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "voice_id": "pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4",
      "text": "I think I know where they came from!",
      "emotion_tag": "[excited realization]",
      "duration_ms": 2240,
      "sha256": "8c1b22ed0def3a3cde0690882b19244cff6eefc09ca0de6875a12b94c62b2814"
    },
    {
      "file": "en/CH04_P04_L004_en.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L004",
      "language": "en",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F03",
      "reading_order": 4,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_015",
      "role": "professor",
      "kind": "science_explanation",
      "voice_id": "pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4",
      "text": "Their DNA is strikingly similar to that of ancient Earth reptiles!",
      "emotion_tag": "[with scientific wonder]",
      "duration_ms": 4800,
      "sha256": "8f24b0766fb0435093a0a1fdb01c7809fe68097938a27b9e2b92da4130fd923a"
    },
    {
      "file": "en/CH04_P04_L005_en.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L005",
      "language": "en",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F04",
      "reading_order": 5,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_015",
      "role": "professor",
      "kind": "flashback_explanation",
      "voice_id": "pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4",
      "text": "65–70 million years ago, giant reptile-like creatures—dinosaurs—roamed Earth.",
      "emotion_tag": "[storytelling, fascinated]",
      "duration_ms": 7520,
      "sha256": "b6640c8a23c31307e6f702f8d31aaf68629c358386e2ed45462de7b11852dd9d"
    },
    {
      "file": "en/CH04_P04_L006_en.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L006",
      "language": "en",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F05",
      "reading_order": 6,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_015",
      "role": "professor",
      "kind": "flashback_explanation",
      "voice_id": "pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4",
      "text": "But around 66 million years ago, an enormous asteroid changed everything. Most dinosaurs vanished, opening new paths for mammals to evolve—and, much later, humans.",
      "emotion_tag": "[serious, thoughtful]",
      "duration_ms": 13360,
      "sha256": "f7cc83ff77932cf3cfc6050d461559083136e093f665ce7e49d036aadd9f252a"
    },
    {
      "file": "pt_BR/CH04_P04_L001_pt_BR.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L001",
      "language": "pt_BR",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F01",
      "reading_order": 1,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_004",
      "role": "narrator",
      "kind": "narration",
      "voice_id": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "Durante a viagem, o professor decidiu examinar as amostras coletadas em Archeon.",
      "emotion_tag": "[with curiosity]",
      "duration_ms": 5040,
      "sha256": "d21d9cecde7c711d7e5e6366022b62981d6d1778f20746ff838572b975a58a0c"
    },
    {
      "file": "pt_BR/CH04_P04_L002_pt_BR.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L002",
      "language": "pt_BR",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F01",
      "reading_order": 2,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_001",
      "role": "mika",
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "voice_id": "XjcBo3s44Dqh64FhOpGk",
      "text": "O que foi?",
      "emotion_tag": "[curious]",
      "duration_ms": 1040,
      "sha256": "ef7759fb1975a4c9daafcf20c1ec7797e54b89cdad6e6c35b7cef89400a35a74"
    },
    {
      "file": "pt_BR/CH04_P04_L003_pt_BR.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L003",
      "language": "pt_BR",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F02",
      "reading_order": 3,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_015",
      "role": "professor",
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "voice_id": "pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4",
      "text": "Acho que já sei de onde eles vieram!",
      "emotion_tag": "[excited realization]",
      "duration_ms": 2560,
      "sha256": "57b850b29e39e225cd4cae3370cc732eddfdfc6b5d10735f8775d805edc6d1f4"
    },
    {
      "file": "pt_BR/CH04_P04_L004_pt_BR.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L004",
      "language": "pt_BR",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F03",
      "reading_order": 4,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_015",
      "role": "professor",
      "kind": "science_explanation",
      "voice_id": "pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4",
      "text": "O DNA deles é surpreendentemente parecido com o de antigos répteis da Terra!",
      "emotion_tag": "[with scientific wonder]",
      "duration_ms": 5440,
      "sha256": "c877a3db77581ff04e1b8e14dff39e48eba4479234c110699a93d960ca8ce7de"
    },
    {
      "file": "pt_BR/CH04_P04_L005_pt_BR.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L005",
      "language": "pt_BR",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F04",
      "reading_order": 5,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_015",
      "role": "professor",
      "kind": "flashback_explanation",
      "voice_id": "pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4",
      "text": "Há 65 a 70 milhões de anos, a Terra era habitada por enormes criaturas semelhantes a lagartos: os dinossauros.",
      "emotion_tag": "[storytelling, fascinated]",
      "duration_ms": 9120,
      "sha256": "edb7b72bd79b941e70adba2458269d475fcb1e007e052b767769edbc6cf943af"
    },
    {
      "file": "pt_BR/CH04_P04_L006_pt_BR.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L006",
      "language": "pt_BR",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F05",
      "reading_order": 6,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_015",
      "role": "professor",
      "kind": "flashback_explanation",
      "voice_id": "pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4",
      "text": "Mas, há cerca de 66 milhões de anos, o impacto de um asteroide gigantesco mudou tudo. A maioria dos dinossauros desapareceu, abrindo novos caminhos para a evolução dos mamíferos e, muito depois, dos humanos.",
      "emotion_tag": "[serious, thoughtful]",
      "duration_ms": 15440,
      "sha256": "9074efab50da06c31a21220508517ca67e6e8c151b03b3a97aebf9fa960af4a8"
    },
    {
      "file": "es/CH04_P04_L001_es.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L001",
      "language": "es",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F01",
      "reading_order": 1,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_004",
      "role": "narrator",
      "kind": "narration",
      "voice_id": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "Durante el viaje, el profesor decidió estudiar las muestras recogidas en Archeon.",
      "emotion_tag": "[with curiosity]",
      "duration_ms": 5040,
      "sha256": "95387ad195204a1078eddb459199eeb0d2223348680cf6a354c4e183fdb3cb2c"
    },
    {
      "file": "es/CH04_P04_L002_es.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L002",
      "language": "es",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F01",
      "reading_order": 2,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_001",
      "role": "mika",
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "voice_id": "XjcBo3s44Dqh64FhOpGk",
      "text": "¿Qué pasa?",
      "emotion_tag": "[curious]",
      "duration_ms": 1040,
      "sha256": "c2e4b1549d13437d3d236a500ff59e6de3bf4cc0442609ac0450913d04ce8708"
    },
    {
      "file": "es/CH04_P04_L003_es.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L003",
      "language": "es",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F02",
      "reading_order": 3,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_015",
      "role": "professor",
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "voice_id": "pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4",
      "text": "¡Creo que ya sé de dónde vienen!",
      "emotion_tag": "[excited realization]",
      "duration_ms": 2240,
      "sha256": "0e441a782f6a3623bf72d123c64ff79a27defa98938c9337437c07fa664e1eeb"
    },
    {
      "file": "es/CH04_P04_L004_es.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L004",
      "language": "es",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F03",
      "reading_order": 4,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_015",
      "role": "professor",
      "kind": "science_explanation",
      "voice_id": "pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4",
      "text": "¡Su ADN se parece muchísimo al de antiguos reptiles de la Tierra!",
      "emotion_tag": "[with scientific wonder]",
      "duration_ms": 4400,
      "sha256": "15ecf563e680f68768816e629ad056f1939012b6534c6691c59bfb23ce805505"
    },
    {
      "file": "es/CH04_P04_L005_es.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L005",
      "language": "es",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F04",
      "reading_order": 5,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_015",
      "role": "professor",
      "kind": "flashback_explanation",
      "voice_id": "pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4",
      "text": "Hace entre 65 y 70 millones de años, enormes criaturas parecidas a lagartos—los dinosaurios—habitaban la Tierra.",
      "emotion_tag": "[storytelling, fascinated]",
      "duration_ms": 9440,
      "sha256": "249131cf3313a947e1256e85159a7d29c189b83caa138cb0d5cb89617f8475b1"
    },
    {
      "file": "es/CH04_P04_L006_es.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L006",
      "language": "es",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F05",
      "reading_order": 6,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_015",
      "role": "professor",
      "kind": "flashback_explanation",
      "voice_id": "pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4",
      "text": "Pero hace unos 66 millones de años, el impacto de un enorme asteroide lo cambió todo. La mayoría de los dinosaurios desapareció y se abrieron nuevos caminos para la evolución de los mamíferos y, mucho después, los humanos.",
      "emotion_tag": "[serious, thoughtful]",
      "duration_ms": 16080,
      "sha256": "95ed28d91130ed22aa14af5469e7b0daaf02417ed3fbc71821df5ad5205dbdb1"
    },
    {
      "file": "fr/CH04_P04_L001_fr.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L001",
      "language": "fr",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F01",
      "reading_order": 1,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_004",
      "role": "narrator",
      "kind": "narration",
      "voice_id": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "Pendant le voyage, le professeur décida d’étudier les échantillons recueillis sur Archéon.",
      "emotion_tag": "[with curiosity]",
      "duration_ms": 5360,
      "sha256": "854d1bfeb3e3b27ec14840f0e4c702ad4261b095641f62e55c0b33f02f6ba03c"
    },
    {
      "file": "fr/CH04_P04_L002_fr.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L002",
      "language": "fr",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F01",
      "reading_order": 2,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_001",
      "role": "mika",
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "voice_id": "XjcBo3s44Dqh64FhOpGk",
      "text": "Qu’y a-t-il ?",
      "emotion_tag": "[curious]",
      "duration_ms": 1040,
      "sha256": "6e80a6b6ed27028e3df4cd3f6a773adc88c58ac43b511167d8eea942ba4d964b"
    },
    {
      "file": "fr/CH04_P04_L003_fr.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L003",
      "language": "fr",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F02",
      "reading_order": 3,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_015",
      "role": "professor",
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "voice_id": "pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4",
      "text": "Je crois savoir d’où ils viennent !",
      "emotion_tag": "[excited realization]",
      "duration_ms": 2240,
      "sha256": "39339763e2676468a088221877c0c9bc04f3fae3e5fff4b9c2e9f4d2a3444a2e"
    },
    {
      "file": "fr/CH04_P04_L004_fr.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L004",
      "language": "fr",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F03",
      "reading_order": 4,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_015",
      "role": "professor",
      "kind": "science_explanation",
      "voice_id": "pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4",
      "text": "Leur ADN ressemble étonnamment à celui d’anciens reptiles terrestres !",
      "emotion_tag": "[with scientific wonder]",
      "duration_ms": 4480,
      "sha256": "eac4737c563d7c8f60bf81ba950cae53e29bf077038c09cebd1e855c4387574e"
    },
    {
      "file": "fr/CH04_P04_L005_fr.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L005",
      "language": "fr",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F04",
      "reading_order": 5,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_015",
      "role": "professor",
      "kind": "flashback_explanation",
      "voice_id": "pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4",
      "text": "Il y a 65 à 70 millions d’années, d’immenses créatures ressemblant à des lézards—les dinosaures—peuplaient la Terre.",
      "emotion_tag": "[storytelling, fascinated]",
      "duration_ms": 8240,
      "sha256": "a56382b9839e676ee1675d9ee583ac881559524e8fb4f1b72a0bda5ed289b961"
    },
    {
      "file": "fr/CH04_P04_L006_fr.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L006",
      "language": "fr",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F05",
      "reading_order": 6,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_015",
      "role": "professor",
      "kind": "flashback_explanation",
      "voice_id": "pqHfZKP75CvOlQylNhV4",
      "text": "Mais il y a environ 66 millions d’années, la chute d’un gigantesque astéroïde a tout bouleversé. La plupart des dinosaures ont disparu, ouvrant de nouvelles voies à l’évolution des mammifères puis, bien plus tard, des humains.",
      "emotion_tag": "[serious, thoughtful]",
      "duration_ms": 13840,
      "sha256": "e074582fb0dc45b339b6da301a123bbf257a4410789cb26344f2221348f7befe"
    },
    {
      "file": "de/CH04_P04_L001_de.mp3",
      "line_id": "CH04_P04_L001",
      "language": "de",
      "frame_id": "CH04_P04_F01",
      "reading_order": 1,
      "speaker_id": "CHR_004",
      "role": "narrator",
      "kind": "narration",
      "voice_id": "JBFqnCBsd6RMkjVDRZzb",
      "text": "Während des Flugs untersuchte der Professor die Proben, die sie auf Archeon gesammelt hatten.",
      "emotion_tag": "[with curiosity]",
      "duration_ms": 5280,
      "sha256": "44aaa7da426965e9a07e586d1cf49f4804729be04482ca55d49f0565fad757c7"
